# Weekly refresh of the type-specimen reference data the tree viewer marks
# tips from (app/services/type_specimen_service.py).
#
# Install for the `tree` user. `crontab <file>` REPLACES the whole crontab, and
# tree already runs the log digest from one, so append rather than install:
#     (crontab -l; cat /var/www/dikarya/ops/cron/dikarya-refresh-type-specimens) | crontab -
# Inspect:  crontab -l
#
# Runs as tree because cache/type_specimens is tree-owned (group dikarya, 2775,
# like cache/blast): tree replaces the MycoMap snapshot, and the web and worker
# processes append GenBank answers to the same directory.
#
# Runs 04:40 UTC every Monday:
#   - mycomap  re-downloads the MycoMap type list (~170 requests, ~1 minute);
#              refuses a snapshot >10% smaller than the last one
#   - genbank  asks NCBI about RefSeq NR_ and type-labelled accessions in jobs
#              from the last 8 days that neither source knows yet
#   - curation asks MycoMap.org's genbank-curation endpoint about every
#              accession in jobs from the last 8 days (~14,000, ~140 requests)
#              and records the types curators flagged there; paced 30 s apart
#              because MycoMap.org rate-limits the endpoint (~75 minutes)
# Exits 1 if a pass failed; the previous data stays in place.
#
# DIKARYA_ENV_FILE points at ~/.dikarya/redis.env (REDIS_URL with the Redis
# password, written by ops/deploy/2026-11-11-redis-auth-nginx-buffers.sh), so
# the curation pass honours the MycoMap.org rate-limit pause the live site
# records in Redis. A missing file is ignored and the pause check fails open.

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

40 4 * * 1 mkdir -p $HOME/.dikarya/type-specimens && cd /var/www/dikarya && DIKARYA_ENV_FILE=$HOME/.dikarya/redis.env /var/www/dikarya/.venv/bin/python /var/www/dikarya/scripts/dikarya_refresh_type_specimens.py --since-days 8 > $HOME/.dikarya/type-specimens/$(date -u +\%Y-\%m-\%d).txt 2>&1; find $HOME/.dikarya/type-specimens -name '*.txt' -mtime +90 -delete
